  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "In case of polar protic solvents, two factors decide the basic character. The positive inductive effect from alkyl groups which increases basicity.<br /><br /><math><msup><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi></mrow></msup><mo>&#62;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi></mrow></msup><mo>&#62;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi></mrow></msup></math> Amine<br /><br />&amp; the Steric Hindrance.&nbsp;<math><msup><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi></mrow></msup><mo>&#62;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>&#160;</mi></mrow></msup><mo>&#62;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>o&#160;</mi></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;<br /><br />Thus, the resultant basic character is determined by taking the above two factors into account.<br /><br />So order will be <math><msup><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi></mrow></msup><mo>&#62;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi></mrow></msup><mo>&#62;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;if methyl group is present as alkyl group otherwise order will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>.<br /><br />In aromatic &amp; Aliphatic: Aliphatic Amine are more basic than aromatic because the lone pair of <math><mi>N</mi></math> is involved in delocalization.<br /><br />So basic character is in the order <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>o</mi></msup><mo>&#62;</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mi>o</mi></msup><mo>&#62;</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>o</mi></msup><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></math><br /><br />So (B) &gt; (A) &gt; (C) &gt; (D)",
